From 60a4ed00cbcfb4eb41c2346352a22f9fb96c72af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ian <ian.laffey@mail.mcgill.ca>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 16:35:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] AP_NavEKF3: gate TAS and sideslip fusion through when
 _has_forced_position
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After the EK3_OPTIONS bit 3 (ExtPosCanBootstrap) external position
bootstrap transitions the filter to AID_ABSOLUTE, the EKF needs to be
able to estimate velocity between companion-supplied position fixes.
Without GPS or any other velocity-bearing sensor, the only available
constraints are airspeed (gives |velocity_NED - wind_NED|) and the
zero-sideslip assumption (gives velocity direction relative to wind).

Stock behaviour gates both TAS fusion and sideslip fusion on
!inhibitWindStates, and setWindMagStateLearningMode keeps wind states
inhibited until |velocity_NED| > 5 m/s — which itself requires those
fusion paths to be running. This circular gate prevents either fusion
from engaging post-bootstrap when there is no real velocity source.

Relax both gates to also fire when _has_forced_position && inFlight,
even while wind states remain inhibited:

  - SelectTasFusion: airspeed innovation updates velocity states.
    Wind state rows of the Kalman gain are zeroed by inhibitWindStates
    elsewhere, so wind state is not corrupted while inhibited. Once
    velocity crosses the 5 m/s threshold, wind learning un-inhibits
    naturally and the full TAS fusion behaviour resumes.

  - SelectBetaDragFusion: sideslip fusion runs, marked f_required so
    it corrects all states (including velocity) rather than only wind.

Importantly, the FuseAirspeed innovation consistency gate is NOT
bypassed. If the pitot fails (blockage, water, electrical fault), bad
airspeed readings still get rejected by the innovation check and the
EKF preserves its only diagnostic for sensor failure under GPS denial.

This patch is part of the Theseus Cyclops EKF integration patch set.
---
 .../AP_NavEKF3/AP_NavEKF3_AirDataFusion.cpp   | 25 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libraries/AP_NavEKF3/AP_NavEKF3_AirDataFusion.cpp b/libraries/AP_NavEKF3/AP_NavEKF3_AirDataFusion.cpp
index c188681f0e..f9986fa618 100644
--- a/libraries/AP_NavEKF3/AP_NavEKF3_AirDataFusion.cpp
+++ b/libraries/AP_NavEKF3/AP_NavEKF3_AirDataFusion.cpp
@@ -205,9 +205,17 @@ void NavEKF3_core::SelectTasFusion()
     // get true airspeed measurement
     readAirSpdData();
 
-    // if the filter is initialised, wind states are not inhibited and we have data to fuse, then perform TAS fusion
-
-    if (tasDataToFuse && statesInitialised && !inhibitWindStates) {
+    // if the filter is initialised, wind states are not inhibited and we have data to fuse, then perform TAS fusion.
+    //
+    // External-position-bootstrap path: also allow TAS fusion when _has_forced_position
+    // is set and the vehicle is in flight, even while wind states are still inhibited.
+    // Wind state Kalman gain rows are zeroed elsewhere by inhibitWindStates, so the
+    // airspeed innovation only updates velocity states. This breaks the stock chicken-
+    // and-egg gate where wind learning needs |velocity|>5 m/s and velocity growth needs
+    // airspeed fusion. Once velocity crosses the threshold, wind un-inhibits naturally
+    // and full wind learning resumes.
+
+    if (tasDataToFuse && statesInitialised && (!inhibitWindStates || (_has_forced_position && inFlight))) {
         FuseAirspeed();
         tasDataToFuse = false;
         prevTasStep_ms = imuSampleTime_ms;
@@ -238,10 +246,17 @@ void NavEKF3_core::SelectBetaDragFusion()
     bool is_dead_reckoning = ((imuSampleTime_ms - lastGpsPosPassTime_ms) > frontend->deadReckonDeclare_ms) &&
                              ((imuSampleTime_ms - lastVelPassTime_ms) > frontend->deadReckonDeclare_ms);
     const bool noYawSensor = !use_compass() && !using_noncompass_for_yaw();
-    const bool f_required = (noYawSensor && (frontend->_betaMask & (1<<1))) || is_dead_reckoning;
+    // External-position-bootstrap: airspeed + sideslip are the only velocity constraints
+    // when there is no GPS, so mark sideslip fusion as required when forced position is
+    // active and we are in flight. This causes the fusion to update all states (including
+    // velocity), not just wind.
+    const bool f_required = (noYawSensor && (frontend->_betaMask & (1<<1))) || is_dead_reckoning ||
+                            (_has_forced_position && inFlight);
 
     // set true when sideslip fusion is feasible (requires zero sideslip assumption to be valid and use of wind states)
-    const bool f_beta_feasible = (assume_zero_sideslip() && !inhibitWindStates);
+    // External-position-bootstrap: also feasible when forced position is active in flight,
+    // even with wind states inhibited (same chicken-and-egg rationale as TAS fusion).
+    const bool f_beta_feasible = (assume_zero_sideslip() && (!inhibitWindStates || (_has_forced_position && inFlight)));
 
     // use synthetic sideslip fusion if feasible, required and enough time has lapsed since the last fusion
     if (f_beta_feasible && f_timeTrigger) {
